      "rationale": "A duration metric is the core axis for a resolution-inefficiency query, giving strong grouping/modeling leverage. However, groundedness is questionable: in the samples opened_at is not shown, and sys_updated_on equals closed_at exactly, yet nonzero values like 6, 16, 10 are produced. The derivation of these day counts is not clearly supported by the visible source text, suggesting reliance on an unseen opened_at (plausible) but unverifiable from evidence."
