  "analytical_usefulness": 0.65,
  "source_groundedness": 0.72,
  "rationale": "The set offers strong core axes (issue_type, resolution_days, assignee averages) directly relevant to diagnosing recurring drivers of resolution inefficiency. However, several columns (is_high_priority, issue_type_frequency, inefficiency_pattern) are redundant with or restatements of other original/added columns, weakening holistic usefulness. Groundedness is generally good for categorical extractions from short_description, but the duration-based columns are only partially verifiable from the evidence: samples show sys_updated_on equal to closed_at with no visible opened_at, yet nonzero day counts and threshold-based 'Delayed_Critical' labels appear, indicating some unverifiable or assumption-driven values."
